WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.941
Throughout the '80s and '90s, Dana Carvey
was a towering presence in comedy, and he

00:00:04.941 --> 00:00:10.480
was the unequalled star of Saturday Night
Live during his 1986 to 1993 tenure.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.560
"Well isn't that special?"

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.039
From the Church Lady to Garth to his unhinged
impressions of politicians like George H.W.

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:22.619
Bush, Carvey was king.

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:26.310
That's great — but what has he been up to
recently?

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.640
Heart problems

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.550
In the '90s, Carvey reported suffering terrible
chest pain.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.270
Doctors discovered that it was related to
blood not flowing properly to his heart.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.270
"Come here, Come here..

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.180
Look at this x-ray, your heart looks like
a pig's a------, look at that thing!"

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.219
Still, the terrible chest pains continued,
even after multiple angioplasties and a double

00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:46.219
bypass.

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:50.710
Further tests revealed that his doctor had
made a terrible mistake: he'd bypassed the

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:51.710
wrong artery.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.640
"Oh no!

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.160
That's not good!

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.620
I'm not happy!"

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:01.860
Carvey had no choice but to repeat the painful
and elaborate double bypass surgery…but

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.449
with a different doctor.

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:09.490
Carvey sued the original heart surgeon for
$7.5 million and settled out of court in 2000.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:15.109
Being the victim of a botched surgery understandably
sidelined Carvey for a while.

00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:16.609
Family man

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:22.409
After he left SNL in 1993, Carvey starred
in a string of what he calls "awful movies",

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:25.849
including Trapped in Paradise and The Master
of Disguise.

00:01:25.849 --> 00:01:30.579
At the time, he realized that he didn't want
to be away from his two very young sons, Dex

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:31.579
and Tom.

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:32.579
He told The A.V.

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:36.649
Club that he even ended up bringing his kids
to the sets of his movies, saying,

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:42.000
"It felt weird and awkward to hand the kid
to a nanny, so that kind of went out the window.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.549
One son had a lot of ear infections, and the
other one got the flu."

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:51.100
During the filming of Wayne's World 2, one
of his sons became upset with his long, blond

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.779
Garth Algar wig and started sobbing.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:58.249
Carvey took those incidents as cues to focus
on his family full-time and moved his wife

00:01:58.249 --> 00:02:03.540
and kids to a "a small town with trees" in
northern California.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.439
Carvey didn't tend to his career for two full
years.

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:11.631
Dex and Tom Carvey are now both in their 20s,
and are both pursuing careers in comedy, just

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.550
like their dad.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.799
Near misses

00:02:14.799 --> 00:02:17.349
He could've been a player on late night TV.

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:22.360
In the early '90s, Late Night host David Letterman
jumped over to CBS to go head-to-head with

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:27.790
The Tonight Show, so NBC tasked SNL creator
and executive producer Lorne Michaels with

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.060
finding a host.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.310
He looked to his SNL cast.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:35.769
Carvey, amiable, versatile, and one of the
most popular cast members in years, was offered

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:36.769
the job.

00:02:36.769 --> 00:02:41.859
NBC thought it was such a lock that they gave
him $1 million, and a Beatles album signed

00:02:41.859 --> 00:02:46.609
by all four Beatles worth $400,000, just to
consider the offer.

00:02:46.609 --> 00:02:50.900
Carvey even landed on the cover of TV Guide
as Letterman's heir apparent.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.069
It took a year for Carvey to decide not to
do Late Night, because he didn't want to commit

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:56.390
to a nightly show.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.930
It wasn't the first time he passed on a job,
either.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:05.430
The 1995 action movie Bad Boys was first offered
to Carvey and his SNL co-star Jon Lovitz.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.430
At the time, it was titled Bulletproof Hearts,
and it could've been a huge hit for Carvey

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.989
at the peak of his fame.

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:15.260
But then director Michael Bay, at the time
best known for making music videos, joined

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:19.650
the project, and convinced producers to make
it a youth-oriented action flick.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.860
Carvey and Lovitz did a screen test, which
Carvey felt was so inappropriate for him that

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.170
he left the movie.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:30.810
Carvey even tried to fall back on one of his
popular recurring SNL sketches: European bodybuilders

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.810
Hans and Franz.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:32.829
"I am Hans…"

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:34.180
"Und I am Franz."

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.760
"And we want to … pump… you up."

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:43.329
SNL writer Robert Smigel worked on the screenplay
for a big-screen adventure with Carvey, Kevin

00:03:43.329 --> 00:03:45.010
Nealon, and Conan O'Brien.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.870
Oh, and it was also a musical.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:52.299
'And then their muscles were going to dance
like 'boom boom, boom boom'… then they're

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:57.290
going to flex and g------ it was gonna be
funny."

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.260
A substantial role was written for Arnold
Schwarzenegger, playing himself as well as

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.860
an Austrian grandmother, but he dropped out
of Hans and Franz: The Girly-Man Dilemma after

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:09.829
the failure of the similarly self-effacing
Last Action Hero.

00:04:09.829 --> 00:04:11.799
After that, the project collapsed.

00:04:11.799 --> 00:04:16.870
These weren't even Carvey's earliest or worst
brushes with the fickle world of Hollywood.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.669
Solo sketches

00:04:18.669 --> 00:04:24.970
Just two years after leaving the comedy confines
of SNL in 1994, Carvey returned to TV with

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.300
The Dana Carvey Show.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.820
While it was critically acclaimed and became
a cult hit among comedy nerds, it was a commercial

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:31.820
disaster.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.970
ABC scheduled it to air immediately after
its family-friendly mega-hit Home Improvement.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:42.020
What they got was wild, weird, and just a
little dark — everything Home Improvement

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.020
wasn't.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:47.580
"The days are rushing by children, it'll be
over before you know it…"

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.020
The show honed the talents of a lot of the
most important comedy writers and performers

00:04:56.030 --> 00:05:01.840
of the last 20 years, including writer Charlie
Kaufman, The Office co-creator Greg Daniels,

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.770
Community writer Dino Stamatopoulos, and head
writer Louis C.K.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.460
And then there were these guys.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:12.280
Ratings dropped after the first episode, and
The Dana Carvey Show was canceled after seven

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.280
weeks.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.000
It took nearly 15 years for Carvey to attempt
sketch comedy again.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.990
In 2010, he and Dana Carvey Show writer Spike
Feresten created a series for Fox called Spoof,

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.930
which was completely pre-taped and didn't
feature any in-studio pieces or a live audience.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.970
Fox paid for a pilot, but opted not to order
it to a full series.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.669
Again, it was very, very weird.

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:44.500
Finally, in 2016, Carvey starred on a game
show befitting his talents.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:49.070
USA's First Impressions with Dana Carvey was
a competition show that sought out America's

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:54.420
most skilled amateur voice impressionist,
with a cash prize of $100,000.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:59.199
Carvey served as the show's "Expert in Residence,"
and both he and Freddie Prinze Jr. judged

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:00.699
and coached the contestants.

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:05.380
Unfortunately, the show was not a huge hit,
and wasn't renewed for a second season.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.180
At least he could still team up with Mike
Myers again, right?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.180
"WRONG!"

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.860
The Evil feud

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:16.590
Mike Myers brought the character of metal-head
TV host Wayne Campbell to Saturday Night Live

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:21.960
when he joined the cast in 1989, and his chemistry
with Dana Carvey seemed natural.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.069
But Carvey had a different take on the relationship,
saying,

00:06:25.069 --> 00:06:27.860
"We were never meant to be a comedy team.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.659
Mike just invited me into the sketch.

00:06:29.659 --> 00:06:32.169
I'm grateful that he did."

00:06:32.169 --> 00:06:38.009
After Wayne and Garth spawned a movie in 1992,
and a sequel in 1993, Myers and Carvey left

00:06:38.009 --> 00:06:44.039
SNL, and everything was fine… until Myers
wrote and starred in Austin Powers: International

00:06:44.039 --> 00:06:45.659
Man of Mystery in 1997.

00:06:45.659 --> 00:06:51.289
The character of Dr. Evil, played by Myers,
was a parody of various James Bond villains,

00:06:51.289 --> 00:06:55.789
but his mannerisms closely reflected those
of SNL creator Lorne Michaels.

00:06:55.789 --> 00:07:00.819
Or, according to Carvey, they more specifically
mirrored Carvey's impression of Michaels,

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:03.379
which he'd do around the offices of SNL.

00:07:03.379 --> 00:07:08.450
Carvey was so miffed at the comedic plagiarism
that he didn't talk to Myers for about a decade.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:13.300
But they've since made up, appearing together
at multiple Wayne's World anniversary screenings.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.050
Dr. Evil said it best:

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:19.530
"It's just so pathetic to see you guys fight
over a silly comedy.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.939
It's like watching two bald men fight over
a comb.

00:07:22.939 --> 00:07:24.879
Who cares…?"

00:07:24.879 --> 00:07:26.759
He's doing stand-up again

00:07:26.759 --> 00:07:31.840
Carvey is mainly known as a sketch comedy
performer and actor in movies of varying success,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:37.080
but when he first got into show business in
the early 1980s, it was as a stand-up comedian.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:41.509
After leaving SNL, he did stand-up here and
there, taping a few specials.

00:07:41.509 --> 00:07:46.260
But he took a pretty long break before starring
in his first new special in nearly a decade,

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.910
Dana Carvey: Straight White Male, 60.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:53.490
Along with Jon Lovitz, he's a comic-in-residence
at The Foundry in Las Vegas, where over the

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:59.210
course of 2017 he'll perform 20 shows of stand-up,
comedy sketches, and musical numbers.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:03.740
So, if you don't see him in movies or on TV,
you know where to find him.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:04.849
Thanks for watching!

00:08:04.849 --> 00:08:07.849
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:10.309
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

